// Module `text`: Text, the stable twin of String (SEM-3): valid UTF-8 published in a
// region, a SeqSpan[u8] (MEM-12). Field legend: API.md, "Reading a contract". Both
// operations are core.md's, restated.
//
// Representation: a reference to a Text counts 16 bytes (MEM-26); its bytes live in a
// region block (count, extent, bytes) charged to the limit current where it was placed
// and freed when the region closes. Text is never frozen and never written (OWN-10,
// MEM-5); `let` copies the reference. Equality and order are `==` and `<` (bytewise).
// Left out: a String view of a Text (`as_string`) and `from_utf8_in`. No core operation
// gives a String view of a Text or of a Bytes view, and a library function cannot make
// one (OWN-20), so both would copy through a temporary String (N2 in SPEC-GAPS).

/// CORE. Length in bytes. Cost: O(1). Ex: `text.len(t)`
pub fn len(t: Text) -> u64

/// CORE. Publishes a copy of s in r.
/// Fails: Error(c) when the block is refused; nothing published.
/// Alloc: one region block of the SeqSpan header plus byte_len(s), rounded to 8, at the
/// current limit; freed when r closes. Cost: O(len). Ex: `let t = text.copy_in(r, s)?`
pub fn copy_in(r: Region, s: String) -> Result[Text in r, Capacity]
